PATCH 314 -- FUN_0000_18dc LOD-model flag setter base-loss (raw host deref of DGROUP data).

FUN_0000_18dc (asm 0x18dc) sets the visibility/dirty bits (|0x22) on a vehicle's LOD-model
sub-object flag records.  DS=DGROUP=0x1c00.  asm-verified vs re_out/fist_dat_image.bin:

  18f9: bx = word[ds:0x2674] (=param_1); bx<<=1; lea bx,[bx+0x26e4]; or [bx+2],0x22   ; flag tbl
  190b: mov di, WORD PTR [bx+0x27f4]            ; di = word[DGROUP:(param_1+0x27f4)]  (WORD read)
  1912: or [si+2],0x22  (si=di+0x40)            ; or byte[DGROUP:(di+0x42)]
  1927: loop 4x: or [si+2],0x22; si+=0x10       ; di+0x46/0x56/0x66/0x76
  192f: or [si+2],0x22                          ; di+0x86
  193a: mov WORD [bx+0x276c],0                  ; word[DGROUP:(param_1+0x276c)] = 0

Ghidra dropped the DGROUP segment base AND typed `di` as a host `int`, emitting the raw host
derefs `*(int *)(DAT_1000_e674 + 0x27f4)` / `*(int *)(param_1 + 0x27f4)`.  With param_1 a small
DGROUP index that address is ~0x27f4 -> SIGSEGV (pattern-init reproduced it: fault 0x27f4,
EIP in 18dc); on the default build the raw derefs land at wild host addresses and OR 0x22 into
uninitialised stack/heap -> the flaky mission-object-flag corruption class.

Fix: reconstruct faithfully -- rebase every DGROUP deref onto V=g_mem+0x1c000, read `di` as a
16-bit word, and 16-bit-wrap every effective address (exactly the asm's `mov di,[bx+0x27f4]`
+ `or byte ptr [si+2]`).  Behaviour-identical structure (the 4x/4x/8x |0x22 walks are the
pristine decompile); only the addressing is corrected.  Sibling flag-walkers 197b/1996/19b9
were already rebased (patch 028); this fixes their dispatcher.

